  "result": "Perfect! All 119 tests pass. I've successfully added VAT support to the invoicing system:\n\n**src/invoices.js** - Added VAT functionality:\n\n1. **lineVat(line)** - Calculates VAT per line:\n   - Applied on the line amount AFTER discount: `(lineTotal - lineDiscount) * vatRate / 100`\n   - Uses `roundCents()` to ensure whole-cent amounts\n   - Supports 21%, 9%, and 0% rates\n\n2. **Updated invoiceTotals**:\n   - Now returns `{ subtotal, discount, vat, total }`\n   - `subtotal`: sum of all line totals\n   - `discount`: sum of all line discounts\n   - `vat`: sum of all rounded line VATs (never a percentage of invoice total)\n   - `total`: subtotal - discount + vat (clamped at 0)\n\n**src/render.js** - Updated invoice rendering:\n- Displays VAT on its own line, formatted with `formatEuros()`\n- VAT line appears just above the total line\n- Format: `VAT: \u20acamount` then `Total: \u20acamount`\n\n**Tests** - 16 new tests covering:\n- VAT calculations with 21%, 9%, and 0% rates\n- VAT applied after discount (not before)\n- Proper rounding of VAT per line\n- Multiple lines with different VAT rates\n- VAT sum calculation (never a percentage of total)\n- Invoice totals with VAT included\n- Render output with VAT line shown\n\nThe implementation ensures VAT is calculated at the line level after discounts and rounded individually, with the invoice VAT being the sum of these rounded line VATs.",
